codex
P2 has a concrete error: shifting by zero is defined, and `(1 << 0) - 1` is already zero. That reduces the count to 468 undefined cases on a 32-bit-`int` host. I also found an Arm reference that lists NOP as an allowed outcome when `msb < lsb`.
